      "alignment": "Chaotic Neutral",
      "type": {
        "value": "monstrosity",
        "subtype": "koopa"
      },
      "cr": 7,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Era sheet: Highsun 1, 955 BF, Peach's Castle.</em> Art and stats describe this figure on the night of the Day Of (events.json <code>highsun_1_955_bf_the_day_of</code>), not the present day of the campaign (1040 BF).</p><p><strong>Scene kit — The Interloper at the Council.</strong> Bowser and his force burst in on a crucial palace meeting. This is a GM scene kit, not a filed event; nothing on this sheet changes the canon record of what happened that night.</p><p>The Koopa King, eighty-five years before the present day: younger, louder and already in the habit of arriving uninvited. The archive puts him inside Peach's Castle on the Day Of and has the guards drag him across a corridor before the night is out — the propaganda that followed hung the assassination on him for a generation.</p><p><strong>Not the player character.</strong> The present-day Bowser is a PC at level 8 in the XP ledger (<code>fvtt-Actor-bowser-kzNSSjAedvhKTfZC.json</code>). This is an era NPC for the council scene; import it beside the PC, never over it. CR 7 keeps him beatable by a room full of guards plus a hero or two, which is what the record says happened.</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
